 *
 * Each command method is tagged @Command("add"), @Command("sub") and so on.
 * dispatch(target, command, a, b) must:
 *
 *   1. Walk target.getClass().getDeclaredMethods().
 *   2. Read the @Command annotation off each one with
 *      method.getAnnotation(Command.class) -- it is null when absent.
 *   3. When the annotation's value() equals command, call setAccessible(true),
 *      invoke the method with (a, b), and return the int result.
 *   4. If no method matches, throw
 *      new IllegalArgumentException("unknown command: " + command).
 *
 * The method NAME is irrelevant -- "add" is handled by plus(), not by a method
 * called add -- and a method with no @Command is never reachable, even if you
 * ask for it by name.
